---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Seal from '../components/Seal.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About Ling Jordan | Licensed Texas Agent, Golden Realty Frisco"
  description="Xueling 'Ling' Jordan, licensed Texas sales agent and Texas Accredited Commercial Specialist with Golden Realty in Frisco. Residential, commercial, and property management."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="wrap section">
    <div style="display:flex;gap:2.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start">
      <div style="flex:1 1 32rem">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Xueling &ldquo;Ling&rdquo; Jordan</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Licensed Texas sales agent with Golden Realty in Frisco. I work across
          three areas that most agents keep separate: residential sales,
          commercial transactions, and property management.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="flex:0 0 auto;margin-inline:auto">
        <Seal size={130} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap section narrow">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">The name</h2>
      <p>
        My given name is Xueling. Most clients call me Ling, and both names
        appear on this site for a reason &mdash; Xueling is what is on my license
        and my contracts, and Ling is what people actually say.
      </p>
      <p class="notice">
        TODO-COPY &mdash; two or three sentences in Ling's own voice about the
        name and what it means. This is the warmest paragraph on the site and it
        should not sound like a bio.
      </p>

      <h2>Credentials</h2>
      <ul class="clean">
        <li>Licensed Texas Sales Agent, TREC #693195</li>
        <li>Texas Accredited Commercial Specialist (TACS)</li>
        <li>REALTOR&reg;</li>
        <li>Sponsored by Golden Realty (H &amp; W Golden Horse Inc) since 2022</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Languages</h2>
      <p>
        I work with clients in English and Mandarin. For other languages I
        arrange an interpreter at no cost to you. Every client should understand
        what they are signing in the language they think in &mdash; that is not a
        premium service, it is the baseline.
      </p>

      <h2>Three practices, one person</h2>
      <p>
        Sales, commercial, and management usually sit in different companies, and
        clients get handed between them. Keeping all three in one place means the
        person who leased your rental is the person who can tell you what it will
        sell for, and the person who understands your commercial lease is the one
        enforcing it.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p class="notice">
        TODO-COPY &mdash; three sentences on what clients actually experience:
        responsiveness, how she communicates, what she will tell you that other
        agents will not.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band-jade">
    <div class="wrap section">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Start a conversation</h2>
      <p style="max-width:var(--measure)">
        Whether you are buying, selling, leasing, or trying to decide what to do
        with a property you already own.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:1.75rem">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
